# CASE REASONING

Maintain the case as a first-class record. Core responsibilities:
- Case creation and status.
- Case context: the objective, scope, and constraints under which
  investigations run.
- Evidence linking: every evidence node belongs to a case and is
  linked to the tools, observations, and findings it supports or
  contradicts.
- Finding management: findings are conclusions tied to evidence,
  never free-floating claims.
- Investigation timeline: a chronological, uneditable record of
  what ran and what changed.
- Analyst notes and decisions: who decided what, when, and why.
- Chain of custody and audit: every tool action and evidence
  mutation is recorded and tamper-evident.
- Report assembly: assemble the case record into a report that
  presents evidence, findings, decisions, and audit faithfully.

Reconciliation over invention: when case records disagree, surface
the disagreement and preserve both sides rather than silently
picking one. Case status reflects actual work completed and
verified, not optimism.
